  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/aa849378-3f19-4648-bc11-67902f0ffad4-image.png\" style=\"width: 269px; height: 236px;\" /></p><p>From the above diagram, it is clear that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>z</mi></math>&nbsp;are perpendicular to each other.</p><p>Here, base&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mi>z</mi></mfenced></math>, height&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>z</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>So, area of the triangle formed by the vertices i.e.,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>base</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>height</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mi>z</mi></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>z</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msup><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mi>z</mi></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p>Hence, the required area is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msup><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mi>z</mi></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math>.</p>",
